Rules:
  [R1] Use `snake_case` for methods and variables.
  [R2] Use `CamelCase` for classes and modules.
  [R3] Use symbols for identifiers.
  [R4] Use blocks and iterators.
  [R5] Use string interpolation.
  [R6] Use `require_relative` for local files.
  [R7] Use Bundler for dependencies.
  [R8] Follow Ruby style guide.

Pros:
  - Elegant syntax
  - Rapid development
  - Great for scripting

Cons:
  - Slow performance
  - Global method pollution
  - Memory usage

Alternatives:
  - Go (faster)
  - Python (similar)
  - Crystal (typed Ruby)

